3: /// <summary>
4: /// TR-MCP-USECASE-018 AC-006 (appended 2026-11-06, "This includes an age, expiry or staleness decision that a
5: /// background callback in the code under test makes"): a settable test clock whose timers never fire on their own.
6: /// The code under test may create timers through <see cref="TimeProvider.CreateTimer"/>; each one is recorded with its
7: /// callback, state, due time and period, and its callback runs only when the test calls <see cref="TriggeredTimer.Fire"/>
8: /// or <see cref="FireAll"/>. So a background cleanup, poll or deadline in the code under test runs exactly where the test
9: /// places it in the scripted trace, and neither real elapsed time nor a wall-clock change can run it.
10: /// </summary>
11: /// <remarks>
12: /// <list type="table">
13: /// <listheader><term>Date</term><description>Requirements; AC; change and reason</description></listheader>
